{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>To sojourn in the land we have come.</b> A temporary dwelling, until the pressure of the famine passes — but not to settle permanently, as our Rabbis interpreted." "<b>For there is no pasture.</b> Say thus: we have come only for the sake of pasture for our flocks — so that Pharaoh should not say, they have come to take a lesson from Joseph. And now let your servants dwell in the land of Goshen, until it pleases HaShem that the famine cease, and we shall return to our land."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:51.836004285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}